The main objective of this paper is to investigate multiple solution phenomena for a specific Kirchhoff type elliptic system of partial differential equations, given by the system: if $n=2$, \begin{equation*}
\begin{cases}
\nabla\cdot(a(x)\nabla u)=\frac{mu^2}{u^p}+f(u)+\phi_1(v),\\
\nabla\cdot(a(x)\nabla v)=\frac{mv^2}{v^p}+f(v)+\phi_2(u),
\end{cases}
\end{equation*}or more generally, when $n\geq 3$, the system becomes \begin{equation*}
\begin{cases}
\nabla\cdot(a(x)\nabla u)=\frac{mu^2}{u^p}+f(u)+\sum_{i=1}^n\phi_i(x,v_i),\\
\nabla\cdot(a(x)\nabla v_i)=\frac{mv^2}{v^p}+f(v_i)+\sum_{i=1}^n\phi_i(x,u_i),
\end{cases}
\end{equation*}where the conditions are that $0<p<1$, $f\in C^0(\mathbb{R}^n)$ with $f(s)\geq \mu
